# Explorable: the picture answers to the user's hand with no round trip.
# A slider scrubs the sun and a pick changes its mood: a higher sun throws a shorter shadow, falling away from the sun, and the sentence says the number
# the drawing shows. A button asks the brain for what it cannot know.

scene figure canvas=square lines=2
line ground 4,78 96,78 thick=1
rect post 29,62 2x16 fill=ink
line shadow 31,78 75,78 stroke=accent thick=2
path sky stroke=none | M5.6 53.1 A26 26 0 0 1 25.5 36.4
circle sun 5.6,53.1 5 fill=accent soft=3
card tools | Try it
slider height 20 80 20 unit=° in=tools | Sun height
pick view tabs in=tools | Day | Dusk | Night
bind height | move sun along=sky
bind height 20..30 | line shadow 31,78 59,78
bind height 30..45 | line shadow 31,78 47,78
bind height 45..60 | line shadow 31,78 40,78
bind height 60..80 | line shadow 31,78 34,78
bind view=dusk | set sun fill=#ff8a4c
bind view=night | set sun fill=dim
say | Sun {height} up: a 2 m post throws a {round(2/tan(rad(height)), 1)} m shadow.
button ask | Why is it longer at dusk?
